# Neutron Smoke Test

The `geisa-imx95` machine selects the NXP Neutron runtime for the FRDM-i.MX95
image. The image provides the Neutron firmware and driver libraries, the
TensorFlow Lite 2.19 Neutron delegate, and the qualification device policy:

    /usr/lib/firmware/NeutronFirmware.elf
    /usr/lib/libNeutronDriver.so
    /usr/lib/libneutron_delegate.so
    /dev/neutron0

The udev rule creates the `neutron` group and grants `geisa` access to the
device with mode `0660`. The delegate and driver manage the firmware lifecycle;
the smoke test does not write remoteproc controls or change device permissions.

## Qualification Fixture

The smoke-test package installs this converted MobileNet model:

    /usr/share/geisa/examples/neutron-smoke/mobilenet_v1_1.0_224_quant_neutron_imx95.tflite

Its SHA-256 is:

    89e1746ebeae7d54dd4e1017e2c8ef52b2b351dd6eb74791dfc50fa11f106198

The recipe verifies this digest during the image build.

## Smoke Test

Run:

    geisa-neutron-smoke-test

The command runs TensorFlow Lite's `benchmark_model` with the external Neutron
delegate and operator profiling enabled. It requires readable runtime files,
writable access to `/dev/neutron0`, the expected fixture digest, a successful
benchmark, nonzero delegated nodes and partitions, and `NeutronDelegate` in the
regular-run profiling section. Delegate errors, unresolved `NeutronGraph`,
permission errors, CPU fallback, and zero delegation fail the test. Residual
host operators such as `SOFTMAX` and `QUANTIZE` are allowed.

This proves that the fixture executed through the Neutron delegate during an
inference run. It is stronger than checking firmware startup, library loading,
or device-node presence alone. Successful output ends with:

    PASS: Neutron accelerated inference verified

Failures end with `FAIL:` and include the captured diagnostic output. The
command is intended as a simple check the NPU is operational and usable and
not intended as any form of performance benchmark.

The Neutron runtime is distributed under NXP's terms. Review [the image
licensing notes](https://github.com/geisa/community/tree/main/platforms/nxp-imx9-yocto/docs/licensing.md)
before distributing an image that includes it.
